{
    "guide_title": "Cupboard Drawer handle Replacement",
    "last_updated": "October 20, 2021",
    "time_estimate": "5 - 10 minutes",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "needs_better_images": true,
    "introduction": "Most handles get broken or wobbly after a while. The handles on drawers in desks, cabinets, and other furniture may break off when a substantial object hits them. Moving furniture from one building to another can also cause this damage if the drawers are not properly secured. In this guide, I will be demonstrating how to repair a broken handle of a wooden cupboard.\nIn step 1 of the guide, you will need to take out the drawer out of the cupboard .Remove the belongings of the drawer before taking out the drawer.",
    "tools_and_materials": {
        "tools": [
            {
                "name": "Phillips #2 Screwdriver",
                "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/products/6-in-1-screwdriver",
                "price": "$6.99",
                "add_to_cart": true
            }
        ]
    },
    "steps": [
        {
            "step_number": 1,
            "step_title": "Handle",
            "images": [
                {
                    "url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/HBvstNaNfkZKSI3I.medium",
                    "alt_text": "Cupboard Drawer handle Replacement, Handle: step 1, image 1 of 1"
                }
            ],
            "text": "Remove the drawer from the cupboard and empty the contents.",
            "links": [
                {
                    "type": "edit",
                    "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/143988/291767"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "step_number": 2,
            "step_title": null,
            "images": [
                {
                    "url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/awVPgxwJ6LjpXsyv.medium",
                    "alt_text": "Cupboard Drawer handle Replacement: step 2, image 1 of 1"
                }
            ],
            "text": "Tighten the good side of the handle by rotating the screwdriver in a clockwise direction.",
            "links": [
                {
                    "type": "edit",
                    "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/143988/291766"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "step_number": 3,
            "step_title": null,
            "images": [],
            "text": "Take a screw with a similar radius of the handle’s hole for the drawer.",
            "links": [
                {
                    "type": "edit",
                    "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/143988/291557"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "step_number": 4,
            "step_title": null,
            "images": [],
            "text": "Line up the hole or holes on the back of the handle with the holes in the front plate of the drawer.\nTake the screw and insert it in the hole at the back of the drawer.",
            "links": [
                {
                    "type": "edit",
                    "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/143988/291558"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "step_number": 5,
            "step_title": null,
            "images": [],
            "text": "Adjust the screw in a way that it stays in a straight line.\nSlowly rotate the screw clockwise and in a straight position so that the handle stays erect.",
            "links": [
                {
                    "type": "edit",
                    "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/143988/291560"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "step_number": 6,
            "step_title": null,
            "images": [],
            "text": "Make sure to check the grip of the handle.",
            "links": [
                {
                    "type": "edit",
                    "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/143988/291561"
                }
            ]
        }
    ],
    "conclusion": "To reassemble your device, follow these instructions in reverse order.",
